  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Baked Monkfish with Ginger",
  "text": "Baked Monkfish with Ginger\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nCooking time: 10 minutes\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n250 g Monkfish,\n\n3 tbsp cup sake,\n\n2 tbsp cup mirin,\n\n3 tbsp dashi,\n\n3 tbsp cup soy sauce,\n\n2 tbsp brown sugar,\n\ncorn flour,\n\n2 spring onions,\n\n1/2 tbsp shredded ginger.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Heat the oven to 180C/Gas 4/350F.\n\n2. Cut fish into pieces and dust with flour.\n\n3. In a small saucepan, add the saki and mirin to a pan, and boil off the alcohol.\n\n4. Reduce the heat then add the soy sauce and sugar and stir until dissolved. Remove from the heat.\n\n5. In a small frying pan over a medium heat, add a little oil, then fry the fish for 1 minute on each side.\n\n5. Add the ginger, spring onion, and the liquids.\n\n6. Put the pan in the oven for 5-7 minutes.",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT10M",
  "recipeYield": "2",
